+# Portable Bluetooth Speaker Comparison
+
+## Finalists
+
+All three finalists weigh no more than 2.2 lb, provide at least 12 hours of advertised battery life, carry at least a one-year warranty, have an IP67-or-better rating, and charge by USB-C. They are ranked by longest battery life, with lower regular price breaking a tie; promotional prices are not used.
+
+| Rank | Model | Regular price | Weight (lb) | Battery (hr) | Warranty | IP rating | Charging | Why it fits |
+|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Bracken Audio TrailBeat 2 | $149 | 1.8 | 20 | 2 years | IP67 | USB-C | Its 20-hour battery ties for the longest among eligible models, and its lower regular price wins that tie while every outdoor-readiness and baseline filter is met. |
+| 2 | Northline Roam 360 | $179 | 2.1 | 20 | 1 year | IP68 | USB-C | It matches the leader's 20-hour battery and exceeds the IP67 floor with IP68 protection, while remaining within the weight and warranty limits. |
+| 3 | Meridian Wave Mini | $119 | 1.5 | 16 | 1 year | IP67 | USB-C | It is the lightest and least expensive eligible finalist, with qualifying battery life, warranty, protection, and charging despite ranking behind the 20-hour models. |
+
+## Recommendation
+
+Choose the Bracken Audio TrailBeat 2 because its 20-hour battery ties the best eligible endurance and its $149 regular price wins the required tiebreaker. It also provides a two-year warranty at a compliant 1.8 lb. The tradeoff is that it costs $30 more and weighs 0.3 lb more than the Meridian Wave Mini.
+
+## Runner-up
+
+The Northline Roam 360 is the runner-up because it pairs the same 20-hour battery life with the strongest listed protection, IP68. However, its $179 regular price is $30 higher than the winner's, and its 2.1 lb weight is the heaviest among the finalists.
